   143	## A11.4 Dependency duty for registered decisions
   144	
   145	When a registered decision changes a parameter (an algorithm, a custody form, a channel, a horizon, a scope, a key),
   146	the owner sweeps the registered texts for sentences whose referent the change alters. Each one is recorded as
   147	amended, superseded, still fitting or open, before the decision's change is treated as complete. An owner decision
   148	that touches a registered parameter is checked against those texts before it is recorded.
   149	
   150	## A11.5 Results of the first sweep (2026-10-28)
   151	
   152	The sweep covered the original, Amendments 1–10, the freeze, the tracker and the author-rulings files
   153	(`docs/reviews/stale-dependencies/SWEEP-2026-10-28.md`). The owner checked each finding against its source. The
   154	review added item 3. The sweep did not read the rest of the frozen specification or the hybrid supplement
   155	(`SWEEP-2026-10-28.md:3-4`, `:20-21`). The Levadura panel read them. Its findings are §A11.3 rows 1, 2, 4–6, 8 and
   156	10–14, §A11.6 and §A11.7.
   157	
   158	**Scope from now on.** Every sweep under §A11.4 reads the frozen specification object in full (`spec.bin`: A9, A10,
   159	PROOF, V1-PROFILE, ENCODING-V1 and the hybrid supplement; `formal/freeze-v1/FREEZE-RECORD.md:16`), as well as the
   160	original, every amendment, the freeze record, the tracker and the author-rulings files.
   161	
   162	1. **H3 (`phase-0-prereg.md:232-248`): not amended.** H3 is a hypothesis with a stated falsifier. Its examples are
   163	   AWS-based, but they do not restrict it to AWS. It is measured over the whole deployed system, every provider
   164	   included. A measurement protocol is recorded before measurement. It covers retained resources (including the
   165	   compliance-locked trail bucket), defines the demonstration and idle periods, and reports the three numbers
   166	   separately. A slot-2 signer and an issuer poller that run through the operating window conflict with "idle
   167	   compute exactly $0". If that or another number fails, H3 is reported as falsified. The operating window is not
   168	   redefined as a demonstration to avoid this.
   169	2. **The slot-2 enforcement boundary: for the author's ruling.** A9.6 requires the final custody implementation to
   170	   be deadline-qualified (`phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md:389-392`). The frozen record keeps "the selected,
   171	   deadline-qualified custody implementation" (`270ca49:docs/V1-PROFILE.md:1024-1025`). It describes it through
   172	   `prototype/policy-signer/` (:1033-1037), which met the deadline on 2026-10-14 (:1038-1040; §14.2 item 5,
   173	   :1429-1435). That qualification stands as historical evidence.
   174	
   175	   Production cannot run the prototype. Instrument code under `prototype/` stays instrument code, and service code
   176	   that ports it must earn its own evidence on its own bytes (`formal/freeze-v1/FREEZE-RECORD.md:62-64`). Nothing an
   177	   instrument produces discharges an obligation (A9:198-200). The E9 ruling R5b (`docs/reviews/e9-packet/AUTHOR-RULINGS.md:54`)
   178	   allows porting instrument code with evidence earned on the resulting bytes. It does not address A9.6's
   179	   deadline-qualified custody, so it does not settle this question. The registered texts do not say whether a
   180	   post-deadline port counts as "the selected, deadline-qualified custody implementation". Each reading keeps a
   181	   different registered text, so the author has to choose.
   182	
   183	   > **AUTHOR RULING: PENDING.**
   184	   >
   185	   > **Option 1: the custody implementation is the custody option and boundary (port permitted; keeps the hybrid).**
   186	   > A signed row says the A9.6 deadline qualification (A9:389-392; `270ca49:docs/V1-PROFILE.md:1024-1025`,
   187	   > `:1429-1435`) attaches to the selected custody option and boundary: GCP Cloud KMS HSM, P-256, non-exportable,
   188	   > behind a queue-pulling policy signer with the A9.6 checks (A9:382-388). The 2026-10-14 instrument run evidenced
   189	   > that option, and A9.2 lets an instrument select among registered branches (A9:198-199). Production runs the
